    <h1>Shingle Roof Cost Per Square Explained</h1>

    <!-- Direct Answer Box -->
    <div class="direct-answer">
      <strong>What is a Roofing Square?</strong> In residential roofing, one "square" is equal to exactly 100 square feet of roof deck surface area. Shingle roof installation costs typically range from <strong>$380 to $580 per square</strong> for standard architectural asphalt, <strong>$850 to $1,400 per square</strong> for stone-coated metal, and <strong>$1,500 to $3,000+ per square</strong> for natural quarried slate.
    </div>

    <h2>How Contractors Calculate Your Total Squares</h2>
    <p>
      Your home's ground-floor footprint is not your roof's actual surface area. Because residential roofs are sloped, calculating the total squares requires applying a <strong>pitch multiplier</strong> and a <strong>waste factor</strong>:
    </p>

    <!-- Pitch Multipliers Table -->
    <h2>1. Roof Pitch Multipliers</h2>
    <p>Steeper roofs have greater surface area and require specialized safety staging, harnesses, and roof jacks, increasing both square footage and labor difficulty:</p>

    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Roof Slope (Pitch)</th>
            <th>Surface Area Multiplier</th>
            <th>Labor Complexity Impact</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for p in costs.perSquareGuide.pitchMultipliers %}
          <tr>
            <td><strong>{{ p.pitch }}</strong></td>
            <td>{{ p.factor }}</td>
            <td>{{ p.laborImpact }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- Waste Allowance Table -->
    <h2>2. Complexity & Cut Waste Allowances</h2>
    <p>Roof valleys, hips, rakes, dormers, and starter courses require cutting shingles to fit angles, generating material waste that must be factored into order quantities:</p>

    <div class="table-responsive">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Roof Architecture Complexity</th>
            <th>Standard Order Waste Factor</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for w in costs.perSquareGuide.wasteFactors %}
          <tr>
            <td><strong>{{ w.roofComplexity }}</strong></td>
            <td><strong>{{ w.allowance }}</strong></td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

